    {
      "id": 94,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        -1700,
        2840
      ],
      "size": [
        920,
        1170
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# LC Skin Beauty ✨\n\nMask-aware skin cooling and brightening for ComfyUI (LC123). Works in **CIELAB** under an auto (or external) skin mask so backgrounds and most clothing stay out of the grade.\n\n---\n\n## Highlights\n\n- **Skin-first, not whole-frame bleach** — correction follows a skin probability mask  \n- **Presets that load the sliders** — pick a starting look, then fine-tune what you see  \n- **Eyes & lips protected** — auto mask soft-excludes dark eyes and strong lip red  \n- **Fabric-aware auto mask** — high local pattern variance is suppressed (prints/weaves)  \n- **Highlight & texture controls** — keep specular and pores from going plastic  \n- **Optional external MASK** — best quality when you already have a face/skin matte  \n- **On-node before/after wipe** — same LC image-FX preview style  \n- **Outputs** — graded `image` + `skin_mask` (inspect or reuse downstream)\n\n---\n\n## Features\n\n| Control | What it does |\n|--------|----------------|\n| **preset** | Starting point (Natural, Light, Fresh, Porcelain, Warm keep, Custom). Loads slider values; then sliders are source of truth. |\n| **strength** | How much of the effect to apply (0 = original, 1 = full, &gt;1 = stronger). |\n| **coolness** | Less yellow / cooler skin (LAB b*). |\n| **brightness** | Overall skin lift (whitening), softened on highlights. |\n| **rosy** | Pink/red flush (LAB a*). Negative = less red. |\n| **evenness** | Local color evening under the mask. |\n| **shadow_lift** | Extra lift in dark skin regions. |\n| **smooth** | Mild softening under the mask. |\n| **texture_preserve** | Caps how much smooth can flatten pores. |\n| **saturation** | Skin chroma under the mask (negative = quieter). |\n| **highlight_protect** | Reduce effect on bright specular skin. |\n| **mask_sensitivity** | Auto mask inclusiveness. |\n| **mask_feather** | Softness of mask edges. |\n| **mask** (optional) | External skin matte; blended with auto for precision. |\n\n---\n\n## Getting the most out of it\n\n| Goal | Suggested approach |\n|------|---------------------|\n| **Natural cleanup** | Preset **Natural**, strength **0.7–1.0**. Leave other sliders as loaded. |\n| **Subtle only** | **Light**, strength **0.5–0.8**. |\n| **Clearer / cooler** | **Fresh** or raise **coolness** slightly; keep **highlight_protect** high. |\n| **Strong studio look** | **Porcelain**, strength **≤1.0**; raise **texture_preserve** if it goes plastic. |\n| **Keep warmth** | **Warm keep**, or lower **coolness** and raise **rosy** a little. |\n| **Less eye/lip change** | Already protected in auto mask; if needed, lower **strength** or use an external mask that excludes eyes/mouth. |\n| **Prints still pick up** | Lower **mask_sensitivity**; inspect **skin_mask** output; or feed a real skin **MASK**. |\n| **Hands / body too weak** | Raise **mask_sensitivity** slightly, or paint/segment those areas into **mask**. |\n| **Plastic skin** | Lower **smooth**, raise **texture_preserve**, ease **evenness**. |\n| **Flat highlights** | Raise **highlight_protect**; ease **brightness**. |\n| **Quality check** | Preview **skin_mask** — white = affected, black = left alone. |\n\n---\n\n## Quick workflow\n\n1. Image → **LC Skin Beauty ✨**  \n2. Choose a **preset** (sliders update)  \n3. Queue once; use the **wipe** to compare  \n4. Adjust **strength** first, then one or two sliders  \n5. Optional: view **skin_mask**; optional: wire an external **MASK**  \n\n---\n\n## Honest limits\n\nAuto mask is **color + structure heuristics**, not a person segmenter. Ornate fabrics and warm bokeh can still leak a little. For critical work, pair with **SAM / face-parse / hand mask** on the **mask** input.\n\n---"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
